A||N||3||jruffsr||Vapor Canister||||1||
Z||000000||jruffsr||12-30-2000||07:20 PM||||I have been tracing a vacuum leak and found that my vapor canister is bad using the test described in the Haynes manual [unable to blow air through manifold vacuum hose with a vacuum on the ported signal hose].  I know I can buy a new canister from the Fierostore but are there other options?   <BR>Can I plug all lines into the canister?<BR>Thanks for the help.<BR>Jeff Ruff<BR>84 2M4<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-30-2000||11:35 PM||||check your local parts stores. the canister is a standard GM item used in many models. You could even grab a used one someplace tho on FWD cars they are usually a pain to get out.<P>If it's not in the parts computer have them check the MotorMite master catalog. MotorMite caries allot of odd bits. They may carry that.<P>I'm glad to hear you even considered replacing it. Most people chuck it without realizing it's not just porotecting the environment but saving them money on gas. In Fiero's case it is also a fire safety device. It retains fumes that could otherwise build up in the engine bay. Can we say BOOM!?<P>No you can't plug all the lines. leave the one to the tank open. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||ka4nkf||12-31-2000||10:23 PM||||Also there is a filter in the bottom of the canister, and you can buy these at auto zone and i am sure at other auto stores. easy to put in.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||01-01-2001||01:40 PM||||If the canister is blocked/broke so it won't pass air on the purge line changing the filter won't help.||||reg||1
